{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 4,
      "name": "Bounce Chain",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "Every bounce is a throw that has to land on something, so each layout is checked against the launch math the tests already use. The pieces are few (ring pads, tilted pads, star pads, sliding pads), so 18 hand-made combinations cover the idea better than a generator would.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "motion kind 'bounce': straight-up throw at a set power (62 = about 9.8 studs high, 75 = about 14 studs high)",
          "look 'trampoline' (the 'cannon' look also exists, but this idea does not use it, so it is never confused with idea 26's aimed cannons)",
          "test helper launchReaches(): checks every gap and rise after a launch",
          "motion 'slide' (moving pads), 'melt' (fades and drops after you land, comes back after 'away' s)",
          "hazard parts that send you back to the start pad"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "Pad height by look: 1, 2 or 3 orange rings on the pad match a low (45), normal (62) or high (75) bounce; only a per-pad 'power' value plus the ring decal",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Tilted pad: bounce gets a sideways or backward 'throw' vector; the pad is a tilted slab (same pitch/tilt piece as idea 14's ramps and idea 6's slope pieces) with a yellow arrow",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Bounce on a moving pad: keep the throw working while the pad slides (client reads the pad's current spot)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Super bounce: press jump within 0.25 s of landing on a pad with a star on it for 1.4x power; a ding and a flash say you got it",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Ring swap: a pad's power switches between 1 ring and 3 rings on idea 18's client beat clock; the rings light up and the drum ticks on each change",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Spent pad: reuse 'melt' with idea 2's 'melt when you leave' trigger, so a pad goes dark and drops once you bounce off it",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Test: extend launchReaches() for sideways/backward throws, star power and ring-swap power (shared with idea 21's launch-height test)",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "Everything that throws you is an orange spring pad: rings show how high (1 low, 3 high), a yellow arrow on a tilted pad shows which way, a star means jump as you land. Each bounce makes a springy boing, higher pads a deeper one. No cannons here: aimed cannons belong to idea 26.",
